# Benchmark: sort a million pseudo-random 31-bit integers with `quicksort`
# from examples/quicksort.chasm. Run as
# `chasm run examples/quicksort.chasm bench/quicksort.chasm`.
# The example's `scrambled` draws from 0 to 999, and so many duplicates
# make its Lomuto partition quadratic; `wide` keeps the whole 31 bits.
# Prints the checksum (the middle element, or -1 if unsorted), then the
# nanoseconds the sort took.

: wide ( i32 -- array i32 )
  :> n
  n array.new ( array i32 ) :> a
  12345 :> x!
  n [ :> i
    x 1103515245 i32.mul 12345 i32.add 0x7FFFFFFF i32.and x!
    a i x array.at!
  ] times
  a ;

: main ( -- )
  1000000 wide :> a
  now :> t0
  a quicksort
  now t0 i64.sub :> ns
  a sorted? [ a 500000 array.at ] [ -1 ] if :> check
  check i32.to-str print " " print ns i64.to-str println ;
